  "body": "From @fantasai in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/765#issuecomment-282113836\r\n\r\n> Testcase: http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4905\r\n> [...]\r\n> Also, one thing to point out here: for form controls the min-content contribution isn't exactly zero, it's UA-defined based on how narrow the form control can actually get. This limitation is probably worth preserving in either case.\r\n\r\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-3/#min-content-zero\r\n\r\nI ran into this as in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4082#issuecomment-551543601 (@MatsPalmgren asked for text entry widgets to be scroll containers).\r\n\r\nIt seems to me HTML should specify for each kind of widget what the minimum content contribution size is. If we want it to be UA-defined, that should still be explicitly spelled out.\r\n\r\n@whatwg/css @whatwg/rendering",
